# THE RUN PROGRAM. One binary, one instruction count, one peak.
#
# Welfare's runtime side used to be twenty-five counters across thirteen
# programs, each normalised against its own baseline and averaged. That shape
# priced a shape guard and a real workload the same way per counter, and it made
# the objective's runtime half an argument about which shelf a benchmark sat on.
# Ruled 2026-09-06: one consolidated program, its retired instructions are run
# speed and its peak bytes are run memory. The per-phase benchmarks all survive
# as diagnostic goldens -- they say WHERE a move came from, and this says
# whether the project came out ahead.
#
# THE MIX. Decode and encode are the bulk, because that is the work the language
# exists for and the claim the front page makes. The stress shapes are here at
# the proportion a program actually meets them: incidental beside the parse, and
# large enough that a pathology in one of them shows.
#
#   decode  98 rounds of lib/json over large.json  1,045,772,072  34.54%
#   encode  90 rounds over the same document        1,042,585,953  34.43%
#   deep    545 trials of the nested grid             188,771,447   6.23%
#   digest  sha256 over a 15,675-byte slice           152,850,246   5.05%
#   index   690,000 characters walked by index        150,623,773   4.97%
#   escape  3,872 lines through the escaper           149,982,432   4.95%
#   pend    50 records with a field left pending      149,607,747   4.94%
#   split   428 characters through the splitter       147,499,570   4.87%
#                                                   -------------  ------
#   the whole program                              3,043,742,734
#
# Decode and encode carry 68.97% between them. The six shapes carry 4.87% to
# 6.23% each, near enough one another that no single pathology can hide behind
# another's noise, and small enough that none of them outweighs the parse.
#
# EVERY FIGURE ABOVE WAS MEASURED, not chosen. Each phase was built alone with
# the other seven set to zero, and its column is that build's total minus the
# empty program's 11,941,844. The eight columns sum to 3,027,693,240 against a
# whole-program 3,043,742,734: the 16,049,494 difference is the file read and
# the one decode that feeds encode, which belong to no phase. Re-measure and
# rewrite this table whenever a repetition count changes.
#
# THE COUNTS ARE NOT ROUND, and that is the point. `split` is quadratic in its
# character count -- 120 characters cost 11.8M and 1,526 cost 1.87 BILLION --
# so a round number chosen for looks put one shape at 39% of the program on the
# first sitting. Each count here is the one that landed its phase on its share.
#
# THE LIBRARY IS THE ONE THAT SHIPS. jsonbench, encodebench and widebench each
# carry a frozen copy of lib/json, deliberately, so a move in their rows is the
# compiler's rather than the library's -- and those three keep doing that job as
# diagnostics. This program imports std/json, because what the project costs to
# run includes the library it ships, and a decode the objective cannot see is a
# decode nobody is paid to improve.
import "./deep"
import "./escape"
import "./index"
import "./pend"
import "./split"
import "std/io"
import "std/json"
import "std/sha256"
import "std/text"

decode_rounds = 98

encode_rounds = 90

deep_trials = 545

pend_cards = 50

escape_lines = 3872

index_chars = 690000

split_chars = 428

digest_bytes = 15675

fn decoded _ 0 sofar
  sofar

fn decoded raw n sofar
  decoded raw (n - 1) (sofar + length (json/decode raw))

fn encoded _ 0 sofar
  sofar

fn encoded doc n sofar
  encoded doc (n - 1) (sofar + length (json/encode doc))

fn digested raw n
  length (sha256/hex (text/bytes (text/slice raw 1 n)))

fn tally raw doc a b
  bulk = decoded raw decode_rounds 0 + encoded doc encode_rounds 0
  shapes = a + b + escape/total escape_lines + index/total index_chars
  bulk + shapes + split/total split_chars + digested raw digest_bytes

fn shaped raw doc a
  pend/total pend_cards . (b -> io/write "runbench {tally raw doc a b}\n")

pub fn run raw
  doc = json/decode raw
  deep/total deep_trials . (a -> shaped raw doc a)
